railroad: the other-copy check in development only (eta's todo n102)

For @blueshed/railroad 0.16.2, at its root: `patch -p1 < railroad-own-signal.patch`. Not applied:
railroad's to take or leave.

0.16 already folds DEV, as n102 asked: an app's production build drops every warning, the .get()
in a render body's among them (3537 -> 2925 B gzipped for `signal` and `mount`, measured as
src/costs.ts measures railroad). What production still carries of development is the check that a
Signal was made by this copy of railroad (`assertOwnSignal`), and its message. A production bundle
is one copy by construction, so this makes the check development's, as the second-copy warning is:
`ownSignal`, null until startDevelopment() sets it, which a production build never calls.

Measured (Bun.build, minified, NODE_ENV "production", gzipped), with railroad 0.16.2:

  signal and mount          2925 -> 2754 B   (-171)
  signal, mount and list    3795 -> 3628 B   (-167)

The cost: a production page handed another copy's Signal renders "[object Object]" where
development throws. railroad's header says "what throws still throws" in production; this would be
the one exception, for a mistake a production bundle cannot make.

--- a/signals.ts
+++ b/signals.ts
